&lt;p&gt;This is a strong development role for someone looking to build breadth and depth in HR, gain exposure to senior stakeholders, and grow confidence handling complex people matters — while being closely supported by an experienced HR Director in a high-impact part of the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To thrive in this role, you&#39;ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in a generalist HR role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid grounding in core HR processes and employee relations, with a desire to deepen your experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational skills, and comfortable handling multiple priorities in a fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
